# Paths are relative to the build context (the repository root).
#
# The name is load-bearing. BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside
# the Dockerfile before it looks for a `.dockerignore` at the root of the
# context, and only this build should be bound by these rules: a root
# `.dockerignore` would apply to anything else built from the root too.
#
# It used to be `docker/.dockerignore`, which no build ever read: the host's
# node_modules was copied over the one `npm ci` had just built for Alpine, and
# once the lockfile moved to Vite 8 the bundle step ran the host's stale Vite 6
# and died looking for a musl binary the host never installs.

**/node_modules
**/venv
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage

# Built in stage 1 — a stale local copy must never win over it.
dist
test-results
playwright-report
android
ios

# Secrets stay out of the image. Config arrives as environment variables; a
# .secrets.toml baked into a layer is readable by anyone who pulls the image.
**/.secrets.toml
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Service-account keys. Stage 1 copies the whole tree but backend/, so a key
# left anywhere in the app lands in the front-end build layer. The final stage only takes
# /build/dist, so it never reaches the pushed image — but a build layer is not
# the place to find out.
**/*firebase-adminsdk*.json
**/*service-account*.json
